preparationGuide:
1. Arrive at the Homam venue by 7:45 AM in traditional attire;
2. Chant Sri Amma Dhyanam and Sri Ganesha Dhyanam collectively;
3. Follow the 15-stotra Parayanam booklet distributed by Amrita Darshanam;
4. Participate in Mahapurnahuti and receive holy sacred ash (vibhuti) and prasadam.

1. Join collective morning assembly for Sri Amma Dhyanam;
2. Participate in Sri Lalita Sahasranama chanting for world harmony;
3. Undertake campus cleaning and environmental tree planting seva;
4. Conclude with collective peace prayer (Om Loka Samastha).

1. Fast throughout the day with light fruits or water;
2. Perform Shiva Linga Abhishekam while chanting Lingashtakam;
3. Offer trifoliate Bilva leaves chanting Sri Bilvashtakam;
4. Recite Shiva Panchakshari and Shiva Tandava Stotram during the midnight vigil;
5. Break fast on the following morning after dawn puja.

1. Cleanse altar and prepare eco-friendly clay Ganesha;
2. Recite Sri Mahaganapathi Dhyanam for Prana Pratishtha;
3. Chant Sri Sankata Nashana Ganesha Stotram and Maha Ganesha Pancharatnam;
4. Offer sweet modakas and seek blessings for intellect and success.

1. Meditate on the spiritual teacher at dawn;
2. Perform Guru Paduka Puja while chanting Sri Guru Paduka Stotram;
3. Recite Sri Guru Stotram and Sri Gurvashtakam;
4. Contemplate Sri Dakshinamurthy Stotram for Vedantic non-dual wisdom.

1. Observe fasting on Ekadashi tithi;
2. Recite Sri Vishnu Sahasranamam in the morning;
3. Chant Sri Venkateswara Stotram and Sri Venkateswara Prapatti;
4. Join community congregational singing of Sri Govinda Namavali;
5. Recite Sri Sudarshana Ashtakam for protection.

1. Illuminate threshold with ghee lamps;
2. Perform Lakshmi-Ganesha puja during Pradosha Muhurta;
3. Chant Sri Mahalakshmi Ashtakam and Ashta Lakshmi Stotram;
4. Recite Sri Vishnu Dwadasa Nama Panjara Stotram for family welfare.

1. Cleanse altar and prepare sacred Varalakshmi Kalasham;
2. Recite Sri Mahalakshmi Ashtakam and Ashta Lakshmi Stotram;
3. Offer 9 types of flowers and prasadam;
4. Tie sacred yellow thread and distribute thamboolam.

1. Fast during the day and decorate altar with butter and flutes;
2. Chant Sri Govinda Namavali and Sri Vishnu Sahasranamam;
3. Sing Krishna bhajans until midnight birth celebration;
4. Offer fresh homemade butter and rock sugar.

1. Set up sacred Golu dolls or Devi altar;
2. Recite Sri Lalita Sahasranama Stotram daily throughout the nine nights;
3. On Durgashtami & Mahanavami, chant Sri Mahalakshmi Ashtakam;
4. Place textbooks before Goddess Saraswati and perform Vidyarambham on Vijayadashami.

1. Light a sesame oil lamp at twilight or midnight;
2. Recite Sri Kalabhairava Ashtakam composed by Adi Shankaracharya;
3. Chant Shiva Panchakshari and meditate on the transcendence of time.

1. Meditate on the fiery, radiant form of Lord Sudarshana;
2. Recite Sri Sudarshana Ashtakam with rhythmic devotion;
3. Chant Sri Vishnu Dwadasa Nama Panjara Stotram for multi-directional protection;
4. Seek divine blessings for moral strength and clarity.

1. Take a sacred morning bath before sunrise;
2. Offer water (Arghyam) to Lord Surya while chanting Gayatri Mantra;
3. Recite Sri Maha Vishnu Stotram and Sri Govinda Namavali;
4. Prepare sweet Pongal and offer thanksgiving to cows and nature.

1. View the auspicious Vishukkani at early dawn;
2. Receive blessings and Vishu Kaineettam from elders;
3. Recite Sri Govinda Namavali and Sri Vishnu Sahasranamam;
4. Share grand festive feast (Vishu Sadya) with campus community.
